import SwiftUI
import KwipMLCore

enum DocumentClassificationLessonContent {
    static let objective="Teach a local classifier to distinguish invoices, contracts and support requests, then classify new documents without retraining.\n\nThe upper canvas reads 36 synthetic text files, joins their category labels, holds out documents and learns TF-IDF features. The lower canvas is a separate prediction path: it needs the classifier package you save after fitting. Nothing is sent to a service."
    static let terms="- **Category:** the one label a document should receive.\n- **TF-IDF:** numbers describing which terms appear and how distinctive they are in Training.\n- **Vocabulary:** the terms learned from Training; new documents reuse this order.\n- **Held-out documents:** examples excluded from fitting so their results test transfer.\n- **Macro F1:** an average of per-category precision/recall balance; each category counts equally.\n- **Class probability:** a model estimate, not guaranteed correctness or unknown-topic detection."
    static let steps=[
        "1. Select [Fit document classifier](kwip-node://control/classifier), then Run Flow. Its tool type is now Prebuilt models; Configure model contains its Data mapping and Algorithm sections. The lower prediction path is not ready until you save and reload a model.\n2. Inspect [Read private documents](kwip-node://data/documents): each file contributes its extracted text and identity.\n3. Inspect [Labels by document](kwip-node://data/labels) and [Match each document to its label](kwip-node://data/join). Labels join by relative filename. Missing or duplicate/conflicting mappings need correction before fitting.\n\nPDF, DOCX, RTF and ODT can also supply extracted text through File Input. Scanned pages need a separate OCR step; reading a file is not proof that text was extracted.",
        "Select [Hold out documents](kwip-node://data/partition). This practice reserves 20% for Validation and 20% for Test, stratified by category. Training learns; Validation measures transfer; Test is not used in this fit.\n\nUse entity/group partitioning for related copies, pages or documents from the same case. Never split pages of one document across populations. Identical text crossing Training and Validation is refused. If a group split leaves a class absent, revise the data/split rather than leaking examples to make the metric look better.",
        "Select [Learn Training-only text features](kwip-node://data/features). Document features uses word n-grams of length one and two with TF-IDF and L2 normalization. Vocabulary and IDF are fitted only on Training. Inspect its Vocabulary output to see the saved terms and weights.\n\nThe table keeps the original text and a count of nonzero terms. The isolated estimator constructs a sparse matrix; the canvas does not expand 20,000 features into 20,000 table columns. This is different from Text encoding's token-ID mode, which remains available for sequence models.",
        "Select [Fit document classifier](kwip-node://control/classifier). Its Output tab is the complete Validation prediction table: use the standard table search, sort and paging controls. Open Metrics for the evaluation. Compare accuracy, macro F1, balanced accuracy and the majority-label baseline. Read the confusion matrix: rows are actual categories and columns are predicted categories. Inspect errors, not just the score.\n\nThe data is deliberately simple and synthetic; its score does not establish quality on your private documents. A convergence warning means the solver reached its limit. C controls inverse regularization: smaller C means stronger regularization. No neural epoch curve or optimizer continuation is implied.",
        "1. Select [Save classifier and text preparation](kwip-node://control/save). Keep Portable package, choose a new destination folder and Save model. Required vocabulary, IDF, class order and coefficients are saved together; source documents are not bundled.\n2. Select [Reload classifier package](kwip-node://control/load), choose Prebuilt / document model package and select that folder.\n3. Select [Classify unseen documents](kwip-node://control/predict), then Run Flow. Its table input comes from [Three unseen documents](kwip-node://data/unseen). No labels are required and no fitting occurs.\n4. Inspect [Inspect document predictions](kwip-node://data/predictions), then save/reopen your project and predict again. The lower path does not require the original training folder.\n\nUse Evaluate labeled documents for a separate labeled population. Output uses the same table viewer as Train; Metrics is separate. Optional review thresholds flag low probabilities without changing the predicted class. Connect predictions to Table Output for explicit CSV, database or API delivery; opening History never repeats a write."
    ]
    static let boundary="One whole document receives one category. This editable practice is unscored. TF-IDF is a useful local baseline, not a pretrained semantic encoder, OCR engine or multi-label model. Apply saves configuration; Run Flow performs the selected operation. Save retains the complete fitted inference pipeline, not optimizer state. Capture controls govern optional samples; required processor/model state and downstream working data are separate."
}

struct DocumentClassificationLearningView:View {
    @ObservedObject var store:WorkspaceStore
    @Environment(\.lessonRailPresented) private var inRail
    var body:some View {
        VStack(alignment:.leading,spacing:16) {
            if !inRail {LessonTextPanel(title:"Private document classification · practice",text:DocumentClassificationLessonContent.objective)}
            Button("Open document classification practice") {_=store.loadComponentWorkflowExample(DocumentClassificationPracticeExample.exampleID,device:"cpu")}.buttonStyle(FlatButtonStyle()).disabled(store.isBusy)
            if !inRail {LessonTextPanel(title:"Try it on the canvas",text:DocumentClassificationLessonContent.steps.joined(separator:"\n\n"))}
        }
    }
}
